{
  "suite": "build-meal-ingredient",
  "description": "Search result or recipe component -> meal row, or null when the server did not supply the food data the row needs. THE CLIENT HOLDS NO FOOD DATA: there is no label->cooking-method table and no label->portion table, and nothing is substituted when a server field is absent. Cooking method comes from an explicit override, else from typicalState — which passes through when it is already a cooking method (boiled/steamed/grilled/roasted/fried), maps \"processed\" to \"raw\" (eaten as sold, no cooking transform), and gives null for the generic \"cooked\" because it does not say how. A null servingG, an unusable typicalState, or a missing portionMeasuredState on a cooked row each return null; the port must skip the item, never invent a weight. WEIGHT SEMANTICS: `measuredState` records whether `quantity` is a raw or a cooked weight, and the yield factor is applied only when a cooked weight is wanted from a raw base. A recipe `quantityG` is always a pre-cooking weight. The generated `id` is excluded from these vectors because it embeds a timestamp.",
  "generatedBy": "pocket-nutrition-sandbox — npm run vectors:build",
